WEBVTT

00:07:28.076 --> 00:07:31.996
They put it deep underground
in the same geological formations

00:07:31.996 --> 00:07:34.756
that the Texas oil
was originally squeezed out of.

00:07:34.836 --> 00:07:36.196
I love the poetry of this.

00:07:36.556 --> 00:07:37.956
It’s like reversing the valve

00:07:37.956 --> 00:07:40.276
and putting the CO2
back where it came from.

00:07:41.116 --> 00:07:43.836
And recent studies have shown
that if you do that,

00:07:43.836 --> 00:07:47.916
98 percent of it will still
be there in 10,000 years.

00:07:48.316 --> 00:07:49.596
When you put it down,

00:07:49.596 --> 00:07:50.596
it stays down.

00:07:51.476 --> 00:07:53.316
This is still a little bit futuristic.

00:07:53.316 --> 00:07:55.436
It’s still in the planning
and design stages,

00:07:55.436 --> 00:07:58.996
but this carbon capture plant
started operating this year.

00:07:59.236 --> 00:08:00.236
A smaller scale,